    "description": "As Ops, I want to know at a glance whether a deal is ready to sync and why it is not, so an absent automatic sync explains itself.\n\n* Sync_Ready__c — formula checkbox testing payload completeness only. Gates EVERY sync, first and subsequent\n\n* Ready_to_Publish__c — formula checkbox adding deal status Active and at least one active link. Gates the FIRST publish ONLY\n\n* Sync_Readiness_Issues__c — formula text listing unmet criteria readably, e.g. 'Missing Vertical; Operator has no External Id'. Displayed beside the button\n\n* Formulas deliberately, not automation: they are always current, so there is no automation that can fail and leave a deal permanently unable to sync\n\nCRITICAL TEST: once a deal has synced successfully, deal-status and link-status changes propagate on Sync_Ready__c ALONE — including switching the deal to Inactive or deactivating its last link. Those are exactly the events the CMS most needs to hear about and must never be filtered out. This is the case most easily broken.\n\n* The manual button remains visible when a deal is not ready but blocks with a message naming the unmet criteria\n\n* Completeness criteria per §4.2: Operator + Operator External Id; Partner + External Id unless the deal is Direct; External_Deal_ID__c; market country, and state where the country requires it; Vertical; plus any commercial terms the CMS needs\n\nEffort: 3-5h. Blocked by §4.2 criteria confirmation and the vertical value set (BUILD-78).\n\nSource: CMS Integration Design v1, §4.2.",
